# {{ exercise_title }}

A CPDSE student lab-exercise app for {{ course_code }}. Part of the lab-exercise-app family:
identical look and behaviour across exercises, durable results across years.

## What it does

Student groups record their measurements for one lab exercise and compare results — within
the class and against previous years.

- Students make a group (just names — no accounts), enter measurements in a guided form, and
  see everyone's latest results on a table and chart.
- A cohort selector including "All years" lets students compare with previous cohorts and
  download a CSV for their own analysis.
- Results are append-only. A mistake is fixed with a correction that supersedes the old
  reading, keeping an honest history. Nothing students do can destroy data.
- An admin area (single password) manages cohorts, groups and exports, and can seed demo
  data. "Resetting for a new class" closes the current cohort and opens a new one — the old
  cohort stays fully visible and exportable.

## How to use it

For students:

- Open the app, go to Groups, add your names, and create or join a group.
- Go to Enter results, choose your group, fill in the form, and submit.
- Go to Results to see the table and chart, switch cohorts, or download the CSV.

For the instructor / admin:

- Open Admin and sign in with the admin password (set via the `ADMIN_PASSWORD` environment
  variable at deploy time).
- Open a cohort for the new class, close it when the class is done, and open the next one.
- Export CSV or Parquet, latest-only or full history, per cohort or across all cohorts.

To change the exercise itself (fields, analysis, instructions), edit only:

```
exercise/schema.py     the measurement fields (form, table, chart, export all follow)
exercise/analysis.py   optional derived statistics
exercise/content.md     the Home-page instructions
```

Run it locally (a writable volume MUST be mounted at the data path):

```
podman build -t {{ project_slug }} .
podman run -p 8000:8000 -v ./lab-data:/asv-mnt/lab-data -e ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me {{ project_slug }}
```

Then open http://localhost:8000

## Tech stack

- Backend: Python 3.11, FastAPI, SQLite (WAL mode), SQLAlchemy 2, Pydantic v2.
- Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript, built to static files and served by the same
  FastAPI process. One container, one process, one port (8000).
- Visual identity: the fixed CPDSE palette and Verdana typography, defined once in
  `frontend/src/theme.css`.

Branding note: this app ships with PLACEHOLDER CPDSE logo SVGs (a simple snake mark and
wordmark in the correct colourways) at `frontend/src/assets/` and `frontend/public/favicon.svg`.
Replace them with the official CPDSE assets from the published logo package before any real
use. Accessibility note: body text is Charcoal on Soft White / Ivory Gold Tint (both meet
WCAG AA); the header title uses Soft White on Forest Green as the identity specifies.

## Dependencies

- A container runtime (Podman or Docker) to build and run the image.
- A persistent, writable volume mounted at the data path — see Access.
- No external services, no database server, no accounts. Python and Node dependencies are
  pinned in `pyproject.toml` and `frontend/package.json`.

